    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0143" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg51"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Harris.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information copy of a
                    letter from the Acting Secretary of the Navy, transmitting a copy of a
                    communication received from the Navy Department from Admiral George Dewey in
                    regard to his visit with the flagship <hi rendition="#italic">Olympia</hi> to
                    Trieste.</p>
                <p>The Department has read the letter with gratification, and you may take a
                    convenient occasion to mention to the foreign office the gratification with
                    which this Government learned of the cordial reception given to the Admiral at
                    Trieste.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d27-a1.xml" xpointer="d27-a1"/>
